Set up the PS buffers for explicit PS and for 64-bit hosts.

- sbr_applied.cpp: with PS signalled explicitly (the extension of a
  mono SBR element), sbr_dec() ran the PS tool without its buffers:
  ps_allocate_decoder() had only run in the implicit branch, and the
  hybrid filter bank pointer was NULL (SEGV in sbr_dec.cpp). The explicit
  branch now allocates them and selects the HQ path, as the other one.
- ps_allocate_decoder.cpp, ps_hybrid_filter_bank_allocation.cpp: the
  pointer arrays are carved out of Int32 buffers and sized in Int32
  words. On a 64-bit host (the fuzzing host) they overlapped and were
  misaligned; they are now aligned, and the serial delay arrays are
  sized as pointers and moved past ptr7 inside the unused right channel.
  The 32-bit firmware layout is unchanged: this is a host artefact, not a
  firmware bug.

Regression input: tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-explicit-ps.bin.

